<title>UK: UK's Ofwat sees water disconnections fall.</title>
<headline>UK's Ofwat sees water disconnections fall.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British water companies cut the number of customers disconnected for non-payment of bills by 46 percent in 1996-97, figures released on Wednesday by regulator Ofwat showed.</p>
<p>Households cut off for not paying their bills fell to 3,148 compared with 5,826 in 1995-96, Ofwat said.</p>
<p>But Ofwat head Ian Byatt said there was &quot;still no room for complacency...disconnection should only be used as a last resort.&quot;</p>
